<speak>Yes, something simple works better. If I say I'll go out for a walk after lunch, I usually do it. If I just say I'll relax, I somehow end up back at the computer. The garden is useful because there's always one small thing to do. I can check a plant, sweep the leaves, or move a pot without turning it into a major project. I'm trying to learn that everything doesn't need an agenda and a follow-up list.</speak>